To be eligible to enter and compete in the Championship , each Driver must:

Have had their Registration Application Form unconditionally accepted by PCA;

Be registered with the CM ;

Be at least seventeen (17) years of age;

Hold a minimum of a valid Motorsport Australia Circuit Licence without Provisional endorsement or equivalent, and;

Complete an online assessment to the satisfaction of the CM .

NOTE: A Driver holding a Licence issued by an ASN other than Motorsport Australia will be eligible to score points in the Championship.

At all times each Automobile must weigh a minimum of 1300 kg, inclusive of.

The judicial camera unit;

In-car camera/s and associated equipment as supplied by the Event Broadcaster;

Radio communication equipment;

Automobile ballast;

Authorised Driver comfort aids; and,

Any additional components fitted to the Automobile in accordance with Regulation T1.13.

NOTE: Automobile Weight excludes any Driver ballast fitted to the Automobile in accordance with Regulation T3.1.2.

It  is  the Competitor's responsibility  to  ensure  that  the  combined  weight  of  the Automobile and  its Driver (including apparel) is a minimum of 1380 kg at all times during the Competition including during scrutineering, on the Track and in Parc Fermé .

The weight of the Automobile must be a minimum of 1295 kg and includes the weight of:

the Automobile with fuel remaining after the session;

the onboard camera system (refer Article S20.1);

the TV production camera or additional weight (refer Article S20.2)

the radio system;

additional weights (excluding the Driver equalisation weight);

any additional parts or systems required to be fitted for development purposes by the TA (refer Article T2.9);

Driver cooling systems approved by the TD.

The weight of the Driver including  any  apparel  required  by  Technical  Appendix  -  Schedule  D  must be a minimum of 85 kg.

If  a Driver and  their  apparel  weighs  less  than  85  kg,  a Driver equalisation  weight  must  be  added  to  the Automobile . For example, if a Driver and their apparel record a weight of 83 kg, a Driver equalisation weight of 2 kg must be added to the Automobile .

The Ballast mounting plate must be installed in the Automobile at all times.

Any Driver equalisation weight or Automobile Ballast weight must be fixed to the top of the mounting plate located in the designated fixing points in the position of the Passenger Seat to the floor of the Cockpit (refer Attachment I ).

Weight may be checked after each official qualifying session and after each race on the scales provided by the CM at each Round .  The weight recorded on these scales will be considered to be fact and will not be the subject of any Appeal or Protest.

Each Automobile that records a weight less than the stipulated minimums will incur a penalty. The penalty for the first breach will be Disqualification from the results of that session. The penalty for any subsequent breach of the minimum weight may include Disqualification from the Round .

